From 18425ce892be7529cf0154f3036181cc33bb2016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:22:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): render neighbor-dependent block shapes

Bedrock omits the Java connection states for redstone wire, fences, and stair corners. Resolve each shape through one shared chunk update path, including multi-block packets and chunk borders, so later block types can use the same refresh mechanism without patching a redstone-only path.

Supply client-neutral FenceBlock geometry recovered from the official
Windows Bedrock 1.26.51.1 executable (build 51061372, protocol 2193).
Collision appends north/south then east/west arms at height 1.5; outline
and camera use rectangular envelopes at heights 1 and 1.5. Convert world
positions to float before adding bounds and omit collapsed physical boxes.

The pinned executable SHA-256 is
537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7.
Verified FenceBlock vtable 0x14e9fd2d0 identifies the concrete subtype;
geometry follows 0x147ac0fa0, 0x147ac0db0 and 0x147ac0eb0. Production
Java bounds match 4096 native cases and 85164 float bit comparisons.
These geometry fixtures supply connection state and vector capacity.

Resolve full snow layers and double slabs explicitly because Java opacity
is zero for those mapped states. Native class constructors identify
FenceGateBlock, SlabBlock and TopSnowBlock through vtable slot 0x390.
Their state hooks at 0x147ac3b70, 0x14a8af490 and 0x1495d8c80 feed the
connection predicate at 0x145675d50. Single slabs clear the category mask;
double slabs retain the default. Snow connects only at its full height.
Gate faces depend on facing and remain independent of open state.
Production Java matches 4096 native partial-neighbor cases and 6034
connected directions. Fixtures supply component defaults, state maps and
region lookup. Complete vanilla registration names, native world
initialization, movement resolution and rendered mesh remain unverified.

Connect to the full horizontal face of stairs, independently of half.
Oak stair factory 0x14c963d20 calls constructor 0x1495c3990, which installs
vtable 0x14ea60ee0. Its component hook prefix at 0x1495c6c50 selects
face bit 5 minus weirdo_direction. Native lookup creates and retains its
default connection component. Production Java matches 4096 native cases
with varying direction, half and unrelated state bits; the original code
rejects the first case. These fixtures supply packed maps, component IDs,
allocator and region lookup, and stop before callback registration.

Connect redstone wire to piston and sticky piston power targets, except their front face, matching the target block behavior. Directional tests cover both piston kinds.

Classify palette entries before resolving connected shapes or refreshing
neighbor borders. Sections containing no fences, stairs, or wire now skip
all coordinate lookups and BlockPosition allocations. Mixed sections only
resolve positions whose original palette entries require connected shapes.
Use each palette's coordinate order and retain the existing native world
lookup, including secondary-layer waterlogging, for final shape resolution.

The previous border path examined up to 24,576 positions per column even
when all four neighboring columns contained only ordinary blocks. Palette
classification also replaces 4,096 inverse state lookups per remapped
section with one lookup per palette entry.

Differential tests compare complete candidate sets in both Bedrock and
Java palette layouts, all four borders, and complete remapped arrays while
shape updates append palette entries. Work-count assertions show ordinary
uniform and mixed sections perform no coordinate reads. The 16 focused
shape and redstone tests pass; changed test Checkstyle passes.
